# Naban, Dean of Iteration: "If a Wizard you control entering causes a triggered ability of a permanent you control to
# trigger, that ability triggers an additional time" (CR 603.2d). Naban is a Wizard itself, so on turn 1 its own entering
# makes Aunt May's "Whenever another creature you control enters, you gain 1 life" trigger twice (20 -> 22). On turn 3
# Emry, Lurker of the Loch, a Wizard, enters: its own "mill four cards" and Aunt May's ability each trigger twice - four
# triggers to order. With all four on the stack Bot2 Lightning Bolts Naban: triggers already put on the stack are not
# undone by the doubler leaving, so Bot1 still mills eight (four twice) and gains 2 (22 -> 24).
# Emry costs {2}{U} less {1} for each of Bot1's two artifacts: {U}, the Island played on turn 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Aunt May
Naban, Dean of Iteration
Emry, Lurker of the Loch
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x15

